{
  "$comment": "Shape templates assigned by rule to whole classes of tests. Curated panels always win; these fill the long tail so every test has a renderable form instead of a blank. They describe the SHAPE of a result (what kind of fields to show), not its values. Like the curated templates they carry no reference ranges and no critical limits. Rules are evaluated in order and the first match wins. A component with units_from_test takes the test's own published units; name_from_test takes the test's name as its label.",
